sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In colonial corals whose corallites are in close contact, the corallites are squeezed into hexagonal prisms; where their sizes vary irregularly they are hexagonal on average, some having fewer and some more than six sides, while loosely bundled corallites stay cylindrical.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Close-packed corallites of varying size are on average hexagonal";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter VII, “The Forms of Tissues, or Cell-Aggregates”; topic “Hexagonal corallites”. Scope: massive versus fasciculate colonial corals (e.g. Lithostrotion, Cyathophyllum, Arachnophyllum)"
}
